# Git Workflow

## Before work

```bash
git fetch && git pull
```

## Commit format

```
<type>(<scope>): <imperative subject ≤ 72 chars>

Optional body: why, not what.
```

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `test`, `docs`, `chore`, `ci`, `perf`

## Rules

- One logical change per commit
- Never `--no-verify` except emergencies
- Commit only when asked or completing an assigned deliverable
- Push after checks pass (type-check, test, build)
- This repo is part of OpenOS — see parent `OpenOS/README.md`

## Hooks

```bash
bash scripts/setup-hooks.sh   # once after clone
```

Pre-commit and pre-push enforce quality — see `pre-commit-enforcement.mdc`.
